# kex: check-only
# A method a trait default provides is still checked for its argument count
# when the receiver's type has typed methods of that name.
#
# Measure is Showable, whose default `to(String)` has no signature of its own
# for Measure, so `1500.gram.to()` was sent to run-time dispatch unchecked:
# the walker printed an empty line and BEAM found no clause (found by
# `make metamorphic-search` on spec/prelude_to_string_dispatch.kex). Measure's
# own `to` overloads all take a target type, so the count is known.
using Units.SI

main do
  IO.printLine(1500.gram.to())
end
